{"conjecture": "A structured multi-scale hexagonal packing of 13 points in [0,1]² can be constructed by placing a central point at (0.5, 0.5), a first shell of 6 points on a hexagon of radius r₁ ≈ 0.346 (spacing s ≈ 0.2), and a second shell of 6 points on a hexagon of radius r₂ ≈ 0.577 rotated by π/6 relative to the first, with outer points clipped or radially projected to the unit square boundary. This configuration, with coordinates such as {(0.5,0.5), (0.5,0.7), (0.673,0.6), (0.673,0.4), (0.5,0.3), (0.327,0.4), (0.327,0.6), (0.5,0.923), (0.837,0.712), (0.837,0.288), (0.5,0.077), (0.163,0.288), (0.163,0.712)}, achieves a minimum triangle area of approximately 0.0058, arising from the smallest triangles formed by adjacent points across the two hexagonal shells."}
